  "ingredients": [
    "3.5 gallons peanut oil for frying",
    "1 (10 pound) whole turkey, neck and giblets removed",
    "1 tablespoon salt, or to taste",
    "1 tablespoon ground black pepper, or to taste"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Heat oil in a large stockpot or turkey fryer to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). Make sure the fryer is located outdoors in a safe area, preferably on dirt or pavement, and far away from buildings, wooden decks, or other objects. Keep a fire extinguisher handy, just in case.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Ensure that the turkey is completely thawed. Cut any extra skin away from the neck area and make sure neck hole is at least 1 inch in diameter.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/Pdnl0vmO0S1g5aN0vCeMMnjE3S0=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/215412-simple-deep-fried-turkey-step-01-1-6caab6afa05b4cc191fc3b27e3f6d598.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/215412/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pat the bird completely dry with paper towels, then rub liberally with salt and pepper on both the outside and the inside.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/XTwCf945eLgik_ffHSa2wwW6Pbg=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/215412-simple-deep-fried-turkey-step-02-2-4395be15ef7d4f07a15b0d61f7f942d1.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/215412/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place turkey into a drain basket, neck-side first. Working slowly and carefully, gently lower the basket into the hot oil to completely cover the turkey.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/mxBR4FvJsplQ4m2bK88Ue8J3JuY=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/215412-simple-deep-fried-turkey-step-03-1-416ec12771e14a06a40ae0ef7f8a8af8.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/215412/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Maintain the temperature of the oil at 350 degrees F (175 degrees C), and cook turkey for 3 1/2 minutes per pound, about 35 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/4OhGVgZw7HcxSl3AP11449cNvDs=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/215412-simple-deep-fried-turkey-step-03-2-0fcb669edf7b44e3b568f2f706de1320.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/215412/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Carefully remove basket from oil, and drain turkey. Insert a meat thermometer into the thickest part of the thigh; the internal temperature must be 180 degrees F (80 degrees C). Allow to rest for 15 minutes before slicing.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/mKsUNh4O86uMRkOO6eFaX3gKXp0=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/215412-simple-deep-fried-turkey-step-03-3-a669e47c052647809e37016f8f42e1db.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/215412/step_06.webp"
    }
  ],
